# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — keep secrets, state, and machine-local Terraform junk out of git.
# =============================================================================

# --- Terraform working dirs & state (NEVER commit) ---------------------------
# State can contain plaintext secrets (CA private key, generated passwords),
# and .terraform/ holds large machine-specific provider binaries.
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*

# Keep the dependency lock file committed for reproducible provider versions.
!**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# --- Secrets in tfvars -------------------------------------------------------
# REAL prod tfvars are never committed. The *.tfvars.example templates ARE
# committed — they carry no real keys. (*.tfvars.example is not matched by
# *.tfvars, so examples stay tracked.)
# NOTE: patterns with a slash are anchored to THIS file's dir (repo root), so the
# bare `environments/prod/...` form did NOT match terraform/environments/...; use
# **/ so real prod tfvars are ignored wherever they live. (.example stays tracked
# — *.tfvars.example is not matched by *.tfvars.)
#
# ENVIRONMENT-NAME-AGNOSTIC ON PURPOSE. This used to enumerate the environments
# (`prod`, then `dev`), and the 2026-09-09 rename dev -> sit + new uat silently
# un-ignored the real tfvars: still untracked, so `git status` looked normal, but
# one `git add -A` away from committing deployment values. A wildcard cannot be
# outrun by the next rename.
**/environments/*/*.tfvars
# Any ad-hoc secrets override files.
*secrets*.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars

# --- Local tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.DS_Store
mywallet.wallet
